<section class="hero-section" style="text-align: left; align-items: flex-start;">
  <p class="hero-tagline" style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">AI Financing Map</p>
  <h1>AI Financing Map</h1>
  <p class="hero-sub" style="max-width: 680px;">
    Who funds whom in the AI build-out — and in what form. Arrows run from
    the payer (outflow) to the recipient (inflow). The same dollar can
    circulate supplier → lab → cloud → supplier, so never sum every row
    into one total.
  </p>
  <p class="ft-hints">
    Drag companies to rearrange &middot; scroll to zoom &middot; click a
    company to highlight its flows &middot; click a link for its details.
    Snapshot: late October 2026.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="{{ '/assets/data/ai-financing-map.json' | cacheBust }}">Download the JSON data</a>
    &middot; Node size is total flow volume (low amounts, non-aggregate rows).
    Dashed links are contingent, “up to”, or LOI amounts — not funded cash.
  </p>
</section>

<section id="afm" data-json="{{ '/assets/data/ai-financing-map.json' | cacheBust }}" aria-label="AI financing graph">
  <div class="afm-controls">
    <div class="afm-row">
      <label>Search company
        <input type="search" id="afm-search" placeholder="e.g. CoreWeave" aria-label="Search company">
      </label>
      <label>Start year from
        <input type="number" id="afm-year-min" aria-label="Minimum start year">
      </label>
      <label>to
        <input type="number" id="afm-year-max" aria-label="Maximum start year">
      </label>
      <button type="button" class="ft-reset" id="afm-reset">Reset filters</button>
    </div>
    <fieldset>
      <legend>Flow type</legend>
      <div class="afm-checks" id="afm-cat"></div>
    </fieldset>
    <fieldset>
      <legend>Money-flow status</legend>
      <div class="afm-checks" id="afm-status"></div>
    </fieldset>
    <fieldset>
      <legend>Confidence</legend>
      <div class="afm-checks" id="afm-conf"></div>
    </fieldset>
    <fieldset>
      <legend>Company type</legend>
      <div class="afm-checks" id="afm-type"></div>
    </fieldset>
    <div class="afm-row">
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="afm-agg"> Include aggregate rows (round / programme / debt totals)</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="afm-comp"> Include component splits</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="afm-labels" checked> Show company labels</label>
    </div>
    <p class="afm-legend" aria-label="Node colours">
      <span><i style="background:#4f46e5"></i>Chip</span>
      <span><i style="background:#0e7490"></i>Hyperscaler</span>
      <span><i style="background:#ea580c"></i>Neocloud</span>
      <span><i style="background:#7c3aed"></i>Lab</span>
      <span><i style="background:#15803d"></i>Investor</span>
      <span><i style="background:#64748b"></i>Lender</span>
      <span><i style="background:#92400e"></i>Developer</span>
      <span><i style="background:#475569"></i>Other</span>
    </p>
  </div>

  <p id="afm-count" role="status">Loading graph…</p>

  <div class="afm-graph">
    <svg id="afm-svg" role="img" aria-label="Force-directed graph of AI financing flows"></svg>
  </div>
  <div id="afm-tooltip" hidden style="position:absolute;z-index:10;max-width:320px;padding:0.5rem 0.75rem;border:1.5px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:8px;background:var(--color-card);font-size:0.9rem;pointer-events:none;"></div>

  <div class="afm-detail" id="afm-detail">
    <p>Select a company or a link for details.</p>
  </div>

  <noscript>
    <p>The graph needs JavaScript. The underlying data is still available as <a href="/assets/data/ai-financing-map.json">JSON</a>.</p>
  </noscript>

  <h2>Filtered links</h2>
  <div class="afm-table-wrap">
    <table class="afm-table" id="afm-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>From (outflow)</th><th>To (inflow)</th><th>Category</th><th>Amount</th><th>Status</th><th>Confidence</th><th>Years</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody></tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Hyperscaler capex — own spend, not lab investment</h2>
  <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted);">Capex definitions differ (leases, fiscal vs calendar years), so use ranges. Do not add capex to lab equity.</p>
  <div class="afm-table-wrap">
    <table class="afm-table" id="afm-capex">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Company</th><th>Year</th><th>Amount</th><th>Status</th><th>Confidence</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody></tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted);">
    Method note: figures are as reported at the dates stated, with “up to”,
    letter-of-intent, and reported amounts kept distinct from funded cash.
    Low-confidence items — including Anthropic’s Series H headline and the
    reported Nvidia Ohio guarantees — need re-tying to a primary announcement
    or filing before use in valuation work. This is a first map, not
    investment advice.
  </p>
</section>

